class_name CellarShelfLayout
extends RefCounted
## ASCII source of "The Cellar Shelf" terrain (scenes/levels/cellar_shelf.tscn).
## The maps are painted into the scene's TileMapLayers by
## scripts/levels/level_builder.gd and the painted tiles are saved in the .tscn
## (so the level stays editable in the editor). Edit the maps here, then rebuild:
##   godot --headless --path game --script res://scripts/levels/level_builder.gd
## The builder only repaints the tile layers; nodes placed in the editor stay.
## Legend: see CellarTiles.paint_ascii ('#' ground, '=' one-way shelf, '^' spike
## art, deco letters). Map line 0 is tile row MAP_TOP; tile row 0 is the main
## floor surface (y = 0 px). Column 0 = x 0 px. 16 px tiles.
## Beat map (tile columns) - see docs/LEVEL_DESIGN_GUIDE.md:
##   0-45    Introduce  flat floor, harmless puddle + Fizz arc (shard 0), 2-tile pit
##   46-140  Develop    shelves clean/sticky, Cork on a sticky stretch, 6-tile dash
##                      gap (sticky take-off, landing +2), shard 1 skill shelf
##   141-169 Breather   Catnap Cushion (x 157 = 46 %) under a window
##   170-238 Twist      two drip-timed 3-tile steps, one-way shelf climb (-6 -> -24),
##                      top corridor, drop-through shelf -> secret pocket (shard 2)
##   239-317 Finale     drop, three jump+dash gaps (12 / 11 / 12) over spikes,
##                      drips on gaps 1 and 3, Cork on the middle platform
##   318-337 Runway     clean run to the Memory Door (x 333)

const MAP_TOP := -31

